 "notes": "Solid purple 'MICROSCOPE Ti/Pt' curve from the top panel of Fig. 3 (constraints_lin.pdf in the e-print), the 95% C.L. upper limit on the linear Damour-Donoghue photon coupling |d_e^(1)| derived by this paper from the MICROSCOPE eta(Pt-Ti;Earth)=(-0.1+/-1.3)e-14 measurement (Table II). Vector paths extracted from the figure PDF; axes calibrated with tick positions (x: log10 m_phi [eV] from -25 to -1, y: log10 |d_e| from +2 to -9), cross-checked against the secondary log10 f_phi [Hz] axis. Curve is flat at d_e~9.9e-5 at low mass and rises steeply above ~1e-14 eV, exiting the plotted frame at d_e=100 near m=6.4e-12 eV (last point). This UFF/fifth-force bound does not assume the scalar is dark matter (paper states UFF constraints are independent of the DM hypothesis), hence dm_density_assumed=null and no density rescaling. Other curves in Fig. 3 (SYRTE Rb/Cs, Dy, Eot-Wash Be/Ti and Cu/Pb) restate previously published limits; the dashed 'MICROSCOPE - osc.' line is a sensitivity estimate, not a constraint. The paper also derives new quadratic-coupling d^(2) limits (Fig. 4), which are outside the canonical linear d_e plane.",
